WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.085 --> 00:00:07.270
Nina rushed into the farmyard. "I'm back!"

2
00:00:07.271 --> 00:00:11.564
"Yay!" Izzie hugged Nina.

3
00:00:11.565 --> 00:00:14.628
"I missed you."

4
00:00:14.629 --> 00:00:18.299
"How was your trip to Korea?" Jason asked.

5
00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:21.414
"Fun!" Nina said.

6
00:00:21.415 --> 00:00:26.513
"My cousin Peter took me to beautiful royal palaces.

7
00:00:26.514 --> 00:00:32.360
We went to Namsan Tower and walked along Cheonggyecheon Stream.

8
00:00:32.361 --> 00:00:38.690
And I ate so many delicious foods."

9
00:00:38.691 --> 00:00:41.798
The kids went inside.

10
00:00:41.799 --> 00:00:47.464
"Speaking of food . . ." Bobby pointed to the recipe screen.

11
00:00:47.465 --> 00:00:51.647
"What are bulgogi cheesesteaks?"

12
00:00:51.648 --> 00:00:56.304
"Nina suggested this recipe," Chef said.

13
00:00:56.305 --> 00:01:01.692
"Peter and I ate beef bulgogi in Korea," Nina said.

14
00:01:01.693 --> 00:01:05.714
"It reminded me of Philly cheesesteaks from home.

15
00:01:05.715 --> 00:01:11.346
So Mom and I made a cheesesteak with bulgogi for him."

16
00:01:11.347 --> 00:01:17.898
Bobby patted his stomach. "Yum! Cheesesteak!"

17
00:01:17.899 --> 00:01:21.539
"First we'll marinate the beef," Chef said.

18
00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:26.007
"Later we'll cook it."

19
00:01:26.008 --> 00:01:30.019
Chef got some meat from the freezer.

20
00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:32.704
"I froze this for thirty minutes.

21
00:01:32.705 --> 00:01:37.423
It will be easier to slice into thin strips."

22
00:01:37.424 --> 00:01:41.750
He began slicing the meat.

23
00:01:41.751 --> 00:01:45.060
The kids started making the marinade.

24
00:01:45.061 --> 00:01:52.230
Nina chopped garlic, and Bobby and Izzie chopped green onions.

25
00:01:52.231 --> 00:01:57.092
Jason mixed together soy sauce, sesame oil, and brown sugar.

26
00:01:57.093 --> 00:02:05.356
Nina added grated pear and black pepper.

27
00:02:05.357 --> 00:02:15.291
"We'll put the meat and marinade in this container," Chef said.

28
00:02:15.292 --> 00:02:19.004
Jason stirred the mixture to coat the meat well.

29
00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:21.617
Then he sealed the container.

30
00:02:21.618 --> 00:02:31.421
"Now it goes into the refrigerator for two hours."

31
00:02:31.422 --> 00:02:35.202
"What's next?" Izzie asked.

32
00:02:35.203 --> 00:02:38.957
"Can I show everyone my photos from Korea?"

33
00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:41.976
Nina held up her phone.

34
00:02:41.977 --> 00:02:51.792
"Sure," Chef said. "After that, we'll weed the garden."

35
00:02:51.793 --> 00:02:55.864
"Time to make the cheesesteaks!" Chef said.

36
00:02:55.865 --> 00:03:00.256
"Finally!" Bobby cheered.

37
00:03:00.257 --> 00:03:03.943
Inside, Chef got out two onions.

38
00:03:03.944 --> 00:03:09.473
"Let's slice these first. We need thin strips."

39
00:03:09.474 --> 00:03:14.469
"Wah!" Bobby said. "I'll try not to cry!"

40
00:03:14.470 --> 00:03:21.958
Everyone laughed and began slicing.

41
00:03:21.959 --> 00:03:26.669
Next Nina put two tablespoons of butter in a pan.

42
00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:29.164
Izzie added the olive oil.

43
00:03:29.165 --> 00:03:35.115
After the butter melted, Chef put in the onions.

44
00:03:35.116 --> 00:03:39.833
The onions turned soft and golden as Chef cooked them.

45
00:03:39.834 --> 00:03:42.455
"Bobby, please get a plate.

46
00:03:42.456 --> 00:03:49.989
We're going to remove the onions from the pan.

47
00:03:49.990 --> 00:03:54.419
Now we'll cook the meat over high heat."

48
00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:58.663
The meat sizzled as Chef dropped it into the hot pan.

49
00:03:58.664 --> 00:04:02.832
Bobby stirred the meat to cook it evenly.

50
00:04:02.833 --> 00:04:07.944
"Now we cut the sandwich rolls," Nina said.

51
00:04:07.945 --> 00:04:11.807
She sliced a long roll in half lengthwise.

52
00:04:11.808 --> 00:04:14.919
"Don't cut the roll all the way through.

53
00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:18.427
It should open like a book."

54
00:04:18.428 --> 00:04:22.176
Everyone carefully sliced their rolls.

55
00:04:22.181 --> 00:04:25.216
Chef topped the meat with the onions.

56
00:04:25.217 --> 00:04:27.954
"What's next, Nina?"

57
00:04:27.955 --> 00:04:35.096
"We add cheese and let it melt.

58
00:04:35.097 --> 00:04:40.049
Then we put the meat mixture on the rolls!"

59
00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:44.426
At last the cheesesteaks were ready.

60
00:04:44.427 --> 00:04:48.316
"Delicious!" Bobby said.

61
00:04:48.317 --> 00:04:50.457
Nina smiled.

62
00:04:50.458 --> 00:04:53.789
But suddenly she felt sad.

63
00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:56.882
Her chin trembled.

64
00:04:56.883 --> 00:05:01.959
"Nina! What's wrong?" Izzie asked.

65
00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:09.129
"I miss Peter. I wish Seoul wasn't so far away."

66
00:05:09.130 --> 00:05:15.763
"Let's send him a photo of us eating bulgogi cheesesteaks!" Jason said.

67
00:05:15.764 --> 00:05:21.602
Nina took out her phone and burst out laughing.

68
00:05:21.603 --> 00:05:28.186
"I just got a text from Peter. Look at the photo he sent!"

69
00:05:28.187 --> 00:05:32.867
Nina's cousin was eating a bulgogi cheesesteak!

70
00:05:32.868 --> 00:05:36.597
"That's a wonderful thing about food," Chef said.

71
00:05:36.598 --> 00:05:41.472
"It brings us together—even when we're far apart."

72
00:05:41.473 --> 00:05:47.697
Nina nodded. "That makes me so happy!"

